---
/**
 * The contact page.
 *
 * Four things, in the order a visitor needs them: a form, how soon a reply
 * comes, a plain email address, and a booking link. The order is deliberate.
 * The form is first because the page is reached by someone who has just
 * decided to act. The response time comes next because it is what stops
 * silence from reading as rejection — the whole point of stating it. The email
 * address follows because a good share of this audience will not type into a
 * web form, and they should not have to hunt for the alternative.
 *
 * The form posts to a function on the host, not to a third-party embed: see
 * `src/components/ContactForm.astro` and `functions/api/contact.ts`.
 *
 * Facts the owner has not supplied — the email address, the booking URL —
 * render as marked placeholders rather than as plausible-looking inventions. A
 * site-wide test asserts that, so neither can ship as a bare blank.
 */
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { type Fact as LegalFact, isUnknown, operator } from '../lib/legal';

/**
 * Widened from the literal type so that `isUnknown` narrows usefully: the page
 * renders a link when the fact is there and a marked placeholder when it is
 * not, and both branches have to type-check.
 */
const email: LegalFact = operator.email;
const booking: LegalFact = operator.bookingUrl;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact — Dr. Wei-Hung Pan"
  description="Send a message about Engineering or Analysis for your study, write to me directly, or book a short call. Expected reply within three working days."
>
  <h1>Contact</h1>

  <p>
    Tell me what you are working on and where the data is stuck. A paragraph is enough, and a rough
    description is more useful to me than a tidy one — I would rather read the real problem than a
    summary of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Send a message</h2>

  <ContactForm locale="en" />

  <h2>How soon you will hear back</h2>

  <p>
    I answer within three working days. A teaching week can stretch that to about a week, and I
    would rather say so than let you wonder. If a week passes with no reply, the message went
    astray rather than being ignored: send it again, or write to the address below.
  </p>

  <h2>Write to me directly</h2>

  <p>
    If you would rather not type into a web form — plenty of people in clinical research would not —
    write to {isUnknown(email) ? <Fact value={email} /> : <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>}.
    It reaches the same mailbox and gets the same reply. Nothing on this site requires you to submit
    a form in order to make contact.
  </p>

  <h2>Book a short call instead</h2>

  <p>
    Twenty minutes on a call usually settles more than three emails. {
      isUnknown(booking) ? (
        <Fact value={booking} />
      ) : (
        <a href={booking}>Pick a time that suits you</a>
      )
    }. Nothing reaches the scheduling service until you follow that link, and the <a
      href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a
    > says what happens once you do.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
